This product includes software developed by third parties, vendored under
src/vendor/ so that the workspace builds as a unit. Their licenses and
copyright notices are preserved in place:

* src/vendor/feetech_ros2_driver
  ros2_control hardware interface for Feetech STS3215 servos.
  Copyright (c) 2024 Jafar Uruç. BSD 3-Clause License.
  https://github.com/JafarAbdi/feetech_ros2_driver

* src/vendor/so101_description
  URDF/Xacro, meshes and RViz configuration for the SO-101 arm.
  Maintained by Dmitri Manajev. Apache License 2.0.

Neither vendored package was modified beyond what is required to build inside
this workspace; any change is visible in this repository's git history.

The ACT policy under act/ is a from-scratch PyTorch reimplementation of the
Action Chunking Transformer, decoupled from HuggingFace LeRobot's version so
that one framework and one checkpoint format serve both training and the
deployed inference node.

The sim2real/ directory is licensed separately under the MIT License (see
sim2real/LICENSE). It contains the Isaac Lab StackCube environment and the
FBC/DBC/DPPO/ResiP agents written by Seongsu Kim, and files adapted from the
Sim-to-Real SO-101 Workshop (Apache License 2.0), which keep their original
SPDX headers.
